<title>USA: Dime Bancorp sets first div in seven years.</title>
<headline>Dime Bancorp sets first div in seven years.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dime Bancorp Inc said it has declared its first dividend in seven years, setting a cash payout of $0.04 per share.</p>
<p>The dividend is to be paid on June 16 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on May 16.</p>
<p>At March 31, Dime had assets of $18.5 billion and deposits of $12.8 billion. Dime is the parent company of Dimes Savings Bank of New York.</p>
</text>
